One of three problems in [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) ([the split](/kb/incidents/4471-split)).
Ticket: [#2](https://github.com/vedhav/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} only="hint" what={{ hint: 'The booking-v3 form hint and its reading disagreed.' }} />

## What happened

The `booking-v3` booking form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People typed the month
first, as told, and the form read the date in the tenant's day-first order. The swap happened
in the form, before the parser saw the date, so the parser fix did not touch it.

Only `form` reports from day-first tenants on `booking-v3`: Alder Physio, Copper Studio and
Pale Harbour. Their app and email reports are [parser](/kb/incidents/4471-parser).

## How to recognise it

Intake can't: it tags from the reporter's browser, and many of these reporters use an `en-US`
browser. Look at the tenant's form (`booking-v3`) and the channel (`form`).

## State

Won't fix: the `booking-v3` form is retired. #4471 closed 5 October.

